 Workarounds
 ===========
 
+KK_WORKAROUND_21
+----------------
+| macOS version: 27.2
+| Metal ticket: FB25499479
+| Metal ticket status: Waiting resolution
+| CTS test failure: None known. Found in Enshrouded (black global illumination)
+| Comments:
+
+The Metal compiler backend miscompiles a 64-bit address whose offset is the
+zero-extension of a 32-bit left shift (LLVM ``zext(shl i32 x, c)``, also
+``mul`` by a power of two and ``add``/``or`` on top of it) when the top ``c``
+bits of ``x`` are set: the shifted-out bits are kept, as if the shift was done
+in 64 bits. The access lands outside the buffer, loads return 0 and stores are
+dropped without a fault. Masking the 32-bit value or ``ulong(off) & 0xFFFFFFFF``
+does not help, the front end folds it back. Seen on M5 Pro.
+
+Worked around by xoring the shared 32-bit base of such an address with a zero
+the compiler cannot see: ``dynamic_buffers[0].zero`` of the root descriptor
+table, loaded once per shader. The xor does not change the value and hides that
+the low 32 bits come from a shift, so the backend keeps the address math in 32
+bits and compiles it correctly. Draws and dispatches that bind no descriptors
+also bind a root table, since the shader reads buffer 0 unconditionally.
+Internal shaders, whose buffer 0 is not the root table, instead rebuild the
+32-bit ``ishl``/``iadd``/``ior``/``imul`` tree under the ``u2u64`` in 64 bits
+and mask the result with ``0xFFFFFFFF``, which is also bit-exact;
+``MESA_KK_WA21_FORM=widen`` selects that form for the driver too. The
+workaround is applied on every macOS version and GPU family.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-11-08: Workaround implemented.
+| 2026-11-09: Reported to Apple.
+
 KK_WORKAROUND_20
 ----------------
 | macOS version: 26

